Losing one's sight or mobility in nh is common, and indeed being blind
is sometimes essential.  But sounds also play a big role in the game,
so becoming deaf would be a big handicap.

How does one become deaf?  Standing too close to an big explosion (land
mine, for example), or being too close to a very loud monster roar (not
sure which monsters would be appropriate).  The shriek of a Shrieker,
some varieties of stun attack, and perhaps a new type of y-class
monster which, when it explodes next to you, does nothing but deafen
you.

How does one regain hearing?  Well, like blindness, not all deafness
would be permanent.  The usual potions and spells, of course, and
eating a dog corpse (since they have such good hearing).  The last
would be a last resort.

Finally, this opens they way for a new tool - earplugs.  The ordinary
kind would just muffle your hearing, so that sounds you would normally
hear ("You hear a door open", "You hear a muttered curse")  would all
become just "You faintly hear something".  A special kind of earplugs -
hearing aids, perhaps - would protect against deafening events but not
otherwise impede hearing.

A Ranger (accustomed to listening for things when tracking) and a Rogue
(listening through doors, etc, when snooping) would have saving chances
against deafening events.

